<Page
  article
  title="Privacy draft: local files, snapshots & future automatic checks"
  description="How the MutualLens preview handles locally imported files, optional IndexedDB snapshots, origin separation, hosting traffic, and disabled advertising."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">PRIVACY · PREVIEW DRAFT</p><h1>
    Your data has context.<br />So should its handling.
  </h1><p class="lede">
    This describes the current preview. It is a product disclosure draft, not a
    claim that legal review has been completed. Updated September 7, 2026.
  </p>
  <h2>Local imports and sample data</h2><p>
    Files selected in the checker are read and compared in your browser. The
    import interface does not upload their contents or account lists to
    MutualLens’s server. Reports remain in memory unless you explicitly choose
    to save a local snapshot or download a file. Synthetic sample records are
    fictional.
  </p><p>
    Closing or refreshing the page loses the current in-memory report. Clearing
    a report removes it from the interface, but is not a secure memory-erasure
    guarantee. Your device and browser may manage memory outside the app’s
    control.
  </p>
  <h2>Optional local snapshots</h2><p>
    Choosing “Save snapshot locally” stores the supplied dataset and provenance
    in IndexedDB on the checker origin. Saving defaults off. Anyone using the
    same browser profile may access these snapshots, so consider shared-device
    access before saving.
  </p><p>
    “Delete all local snapshots” clears the app’s snapshot store on that checker
    origin. It cannot remove files you downloaded, copies in another browser
    profile, browser backups, or data stored by other services. Browser settings
    may also clear local data without preserving a backup.
  </p>
  <h2>Automatic checks</h2><p>
    Automatic acquisition is unavailable. The preview requests the checker’s
    capability status; it does not start an Instagram scan or send the username
    field to an acquisition provider.
  </p><p>
    If a future automatic integration is approved, MutualLens’s backend and its
    provider would process the requested account and returned relationship data.
    That workflow would not be entirely on-device. Its provider, retention,
    operational logging, and access controls must be disclosed and reviewed
    before activation.
  </p>
  <h2>Separate origins</h2><p>
    The public pages and checker use different browser origins. The public pages
    cannot ordinarily read the checker’s DOM or IndexedDB under the browser’s
    same-origin protections. Navigation links do not carry usernames, graph
    data, or session tokens. Clicking an external Instagram profile link takes
    you to Instagram under its own policies.
  </p>
  <h2>Website requests and hosting</h2><p>
    Opening either website sends normal network requests to its hosting
    provider. Infrastructure may process IP addresses, request metadata, and
    security logs. The preview does not claim that there is no infrastructure
    data processing. The application avoids graph data and target usernames in
    URLs, and it contains no marketing analytics, session replay, or social
    embeds.
  </p>
  <h2>Advertising and consent</h2><p>
    Ads are disabled everywhere in the preview, with no advertising-network
    scripts loaded. A future public-content advertising launch needs actual
    publisher approval and identifiers, appropriate consent configuration, and
    completed operator disclosures. The checker will remain ad-free.
  </p>
  <h2>Contact and open items</h2><p>
    The project owner is Arhaan Aggarwal. A dedicated private support or
    privacy-request channel has not yet been supplied and is a public-launch
    dependency. <a href="/contact/">The contact page</a> links to public project feedback;
    do not put personal data or account exports there.
  </p>
</Page>
